@* A line of fields in a form (2026-11-22): its own row inside the form's row, so the next group always starts on a new line (this
   replaced the AppInputFill fillers). The fields keep their Width columns, and stack below the md breakpoint. The fields
   are aligned at the bottom, so a long label may wrap to two lines in a narrow field and the input boxes still line up. *@
<div class="col-12">
    <div class="row g-3 align-items-end">
        @ChildContent
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}